From db9d5819cf04a9ebd042d79514535ba73dd848af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Live Pick 7 table: everyone on 0 the moment they pick,
 optimistic updates, remove team
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- New derived table (lib/league/pick7Table.ts) lists every account in one of
  three states: no_pick (unranked, shows "–"), picked (ranked, from 0 points)
  and needs_fix (old pre-formation seven). Points are never stored: they are
  the sum of played rounds, so a new pick is 0, edits before the deadline
  can't move points, and a removed seven keeps what it already earned.
- Ranking: points desc, hits desc (shared rank), then earliest first pick.
- GET /api/pick7/table (no-store) serves names, status and points only;
  picks stay hidden until the week locks.
- DELETE /api/me/squad + clearSquad(): removes the standing seven (audited as
  squad.clear); it isn't entered at later draws. currentSquad/squadAt treat a
  removed seven as no team everywhere (banner, reminders, draw counts).
- <Pick7Table>: server-rendered rows, optimistic "Saving…" row the instant the
  picker saves or removes, rollback on error, refetch on confirm, 15 s polling
  while visible, refetch on focus, and cross-tab refresh via BroadcastChannel.
- Shown on My Team and on /table (now visible before any match is played).
- "Remove my team" two-step button in the picker.

Tests: 85 (8 new in lib/league/pick7Table.test.ts).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PtuBR2yKPy8UddCaB5RWRB
